  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Regain full lawmaking supremacy and full control of immigration/borders; exit single market/customs union; +20,000 police, restore stop-and-search, +7,000 prison officers, tougher prison controls; defence spend 2%+£1bn/yr, +20,000 personnel, independent nuclear deterrent, strong veterans’ guarantees; target balanced net migration with points/work‑permit system and 5‑year contributions before most benefits; UK‑first job advertising; NHS +£9bn/yr, social care +£2bn/yr, mental health +£500m/yr; 'one law for all', disband parallel legal councils, ban face coverings; crack down on multinational profit‑shifting. TEXT_F: Strong care/equality focus—>£30bn NHS, ring‑fenced mental health, National Care Service, social housing, end rough sleeping, ban zero‑hours, £10 Living Wage, scrap tuition fees, restore maintenance grants; internationalist stance—maintain 0.7% aid, guarantee EU nationals’ rights, human‑rights‑led foreign policy; some authority measures (10,000 more police) but also review Prevent and broaden devolution/votes at 16.",
